Other News of Note this week #ONN
⚖️SEC provides guidance on staking & drops the Binance lawsuit; 
📜a new & improved draft of the crypto market structure bill is released; 
🇸🇻the IMF says “efforts will continue” to ensure that El Salvador does not continue to accumulate Bitcoin; 
🧑‍⚖️a judge overturned three convictions of Mango Markets explorer Avraham Eisenberg, citing venue issues; 
🇺🇸the US Labor Department reversed its 2022 cautionary language regarding crypto in 401Ks; 
💰Cantor Fitzgerald kicked off a $2B bitcoin-backed lending program by financing FalconX and (my former company!) Maple Finance, also launches gold-hedged bitcoin fund; 
🌏Dubai launches a blockchain-based real estate platform, allowing UAE residents to buy $540 property fractions recorded on the XRP ledger; 
🌍ECB policymaker warns that crypto losses could harm confidence in banks; 
🇵🇰Pakistan’s crypto council lead announces plans to establish a government-led Bitcoin reserve; 
💲Circle moves forward with its IPO despite acquisition rumors, planning to raise $600M at a valuation of $5.4B - BlackRock to buy 10% of the shares; 
💸Trump Media & Technology Group denies a FT report that they’re planning to raise $3B to buy Bitcoin, and then confirms it the next day at $2.5B; 
💻Google researchers say that it may be 20x easier for quantum computers to break Bitcoin encryption methods (FYI, STARK proofs are quantum-resistant); 
🇫🇷EthCC shores up security as crypto kidnappings increase; 
🎰while speaking at Bitcoin Vegas, J.D. Vance says that the administration will fire anti-crypto regulators; 
🫂co-founder Mihailo Bjelic steps down from the Polygon Foundation board and Polygon labs; 
📈the Axiom trading platform records $100M in revenue in four months; 
💵SharpLink Gaming announced a $425M raise, led by Consensys with Joe Lubin as the future board chair, to establish ETH as its primary treasury reserve asset (@StarkWareLtd is an investor); 
🤑Strive Asset Management raises a whopping $750M to support a Bitcoin-focused strategy; 
🧓Michael Saylor cites security concerns in rejecting onchain proof of reserves for Strategy, relying on audited financials as the institutional standard; 
🇦🇷in response to an Argentinian court order, Circle freezes $57M of USDC; 
🎮GameStop adds 4,710 BTC to its treasury; 
🇷🇺Bank of Russia says financial institutions can offer crypto instruments to qualified investors; 
🇹🇭Thailand blocking a slew of unlicensed exchanges AI

